    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80-a1">

                <pb facs="0213" n="117" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg117"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    60.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Rivas to Mr.
                            Williamson</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-11"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 11,
                        1873</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to your
                    excellency the inclosed communication, which under this date I address to the
                    minister of foreign relations of Costa Rica, in answer to the circular-note
                    which he addressed to the diplomatic and consular bodies on the 24th of October
                    last.</p>
                <p>Requesting your excellency to bring this document to the knowledge of your
                    Government, I have the honor to subscribe myself your excellency’s very humble
                    servant,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. H. RIVAS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
